            <ArticleTitle>Asymptomatic ureteral varices: detection by Doppler sonography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>353-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Retroperitoneal ectatic or varicose veins may cause ureteral extrinsic pressure defects. Doppler sonography may be helpful in the characterization of these vascular lesions. We report the sonographic findings in a case of asymptomatic idiopathic left ureteral varices.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
